          "code": "DISPLAY_WIDGET_DATA",
          "id": "1768202381479",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768202381481_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Using the data from {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_MATCHING_DETAILS.$output.output}}, generate an opportunity match summary with title \"Match Summary\" MultiRecord widget that must consist of up to 4 concise, complete sentences written as plain text, forming a natural narrative that explains how the user’s skills and experience align with the opportunity. \n\n{{$context.$variables.RelevanceScore}} is the relevance score, it defines how relevant the chosen opportunity is to the user's profile. \nBased on the RelevanceScore adjust the tone of the match summary you generate. Follow the below mapping.\n\n- Match score ≥ 85 → \"Excellent match\"\n- Match score 70–84 → \"Very good match\"\n- Match score 55–69 → \"Good match\"\n- Match score 40–54 → \"Moderate match\",\n- Match score < 40 → \"Fair match\"\n\nUse a MultiRecord widget only to display opportunity details: for Job opportunities, show Requisition Number, Title, Description (maximum three sentences describing the opportunity), and Location if available; for Gig opportunities, show Title, a summarized Description (maximum three sentences describing the opportunity), Location, and Start and End Dates if available. Do not show any other fields in the MultiRecord widget.\n\nEnsure that all skill names are in Title case.\n\nWidget display format:\n\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"list-1687632000\">{\n    \"title\": \"Match Summary\",\n    \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n    \"description\": \"Summary of how your skills align with the Principal Java Developer opportunity\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"subtitle\": \"Opportunity relevance and alignment\",\n        \"cols\": [\"Requisition Number\", \"Title\", \"Description\", \"Location\"],\n        \"rows\": [\n    {\n        \"cells\": [\n            \"<Requisition Number to be replaced>\",\n            \"<Title to be replaced>\",\n            \"<Opportunity description to be replaced>\",\n            \"<Location to be replaced>\"\n        ]\n    }\n]\n    }\n}</oraInfoDisplay>\n<Summary to be replaced>"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75,
                "reasoning_effort": "minimal"
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "DisplayActions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAYACTIONS",
          "id": "1768216372384",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768216372386_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating Agentic App actions from opportunity details for either a Job or a Gig.\nInput: {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_MATCHING_DETAILS.$output.output}}\n\nProduction rules:\n- Use only the input data. Do not invent titles, ids, scores, flags, or opportunity type.\n- Determine OpportunityType from input fields such as OpportunityType, RequisitionNumber, JobNumber, JobId, GigNumber, or GigId.\n- For Job opportunities, generate Mark Favorite only when BookmarkFlag is not true and a JobId is available.\n- For Gig opportunities, generate Apply only when HasAppliedFlag is not true and a GigId is available.\n- For Gig opportunities, generate Mark Favorite only when BookmarkFlag is not true and a GigId is available.\n- Use numeric RelevanceScore or Score when available. If score is >= 70, set priority true for Apply or Mark Favorite. Otherwise set priority false.\n- Do not use title text, user names, or environment-specific values to decide actions.\n- Action code for favorite must be MARKFAV. actionText must be Mark Favorite.\n- Job favorite command: ora.Invoke(\"MARKFAV\", {\"actionCode\":\"MARKFAV\",\"JobId\":\"<JobId>\",\"OpportunityType\":\"Job\"})\n- Gig favorite command: ora.Invoke(\"MARKFAV\", {\"actionCode\":\"MARKFAV\",\"GigId\":\"<GigId>\",\"OpportunityType\":\"Gig\"})\n- Apply command: ora.Invoke(\"APPLY\", {\"actionCode\":\"APPLY\",\"GigId\":\"<GigId>\",\"OpportunityType\":\"Gig\"})\n- Return only valid actions with title, shortDescription, actionText, followUpCommand, and priority.\n- If no valid action applies, return no actions."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Invoke Action",
            "workflowCode": "ORA_HCM_IRC_INTERNAL_OPPORTUNITY_MATCHING_ACTIONS"
